    <item>
      <title>1-Al-Fātiḥah</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/quran/01-fatihah/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/quran/01-fatihah/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;-quran-syllabus-sūrah-al-fātiḥah&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  🕋 Qur’an Syllabus: &lt;strong&gt;Sūrah al-Fātiḥah&lt;/strong&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-quran-syllabus-s%c5%abrah-al-f%c4%81ti%e1%b8%a5ah&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-surah-overview&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  📖 Surah Overview&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-surah-overview&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Name:&lt;/strong&gt; Sūrah al-Fātiḥah (The Opening)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position in Qur’an:&lt;/strong&gt; 1st Surah&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verses:&lt;/strong&gt; 7 (Āyāt)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revelation:&lt;/strong&gt; Makkiyyah&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-surah-fatiha&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  📜 Surah Fatiha&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-surah-fatiha&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;ٱلْـحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;ٱلرَّحْمَـٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;مَـٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;strong&gt;صِرَٰطَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-learning-objectives&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  🌟 Learning Objectives&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-learning-objectives&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Memorise the Sūrah with correct Tajwīd&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Understand the meaning of key words and phrases&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Reflect on the central themes of guidance, mercy, and worship&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-memorisation-strategy&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  📝 Memorisation Strategy&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-memorisation-strategy&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Repeat each verse multiple times&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Recite with a teacher or parent to ensure correct pronunciation&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Listen to recitation by qualified Qāriʾ&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Practise regularly in small sections&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-key-vocabulary&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  🧠 Key Vocabulary&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-key-vocabulary&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ٱلْـحَمْدُ&lt;/strong&gt; – All praise&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;رَبِّ&lt;/strong&gt; – Lord, Sustainer&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ٱلرَّحْمَـٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ&lt;/strong&gt; – The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;مَـٰلِكِ&lt;/strong&gt; – Master&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ٱهْدِنَا&lt;/strong&gt; – Guide us&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ&lt;/strong&gt; – The straight path&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-reflection&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  💭 Reflection&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-reflection&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Sūrah al-Fātiḥah is a powerful duʿā and the opening chapter of the Qur’an. It expresses our need for Allah’s guidance and affirms His mercy and lordship. It is recited in every unit of prayer (ṣalāh), making its memorisation and understanding essential for all Muslims.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Arabic Language</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/arabic/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Jun 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/arabic/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;arabic-language-curriculum-overview&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Arabic language Curriculum Overview&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#arabic-language-curriculum-overview&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our Arabic language curriculum is based on the &lt;strong&gt;Kitābī Series&lt;/strong&gt;, a progressive, child-friendly programme designed to build proficiency in reading, writing, listening, and speaking Arabic. The curriculum focuses on grammar (&lt;em&gt;naḥw&lt;/em&gt;), vocabulary, sentence structure, and comprehension through engaging themes and structured progression.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;objectives&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Objectives&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#objectives&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;To introduce and reinforce Arabic reading and writing skills.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;To build a strong vocabulary base through thematic learning.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;To develop grammar understanding in context (&lt;em&gt;naḥw&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;ṣarf&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;To promote listening and speaking fluency.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;To connect students to Qur’ānic and classical Arabic.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;class-breakdown&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  Class Breakdown&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#class-breakdown&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;class-1-ages-56&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;strong&gt;Class 1 (Ages 5–6)&lt;/strong&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#class-1-ages-56&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Based on: Kitābī 1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Curriculum Overview</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Jun 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;-crescent-school--curriculum-overview&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  📚 Crescent School – Curriculum Overview&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-crescent-school--curriculum-overview&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;At Crescent School, we are dedicated to delivering a well-rounded curriculum that promotes both academic progress and moral development. Our aim is to nurture confident, respectful, and knowledgeable students with a strong foundation in ethical values and cultural understanding.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We offer a combination of &lt;strong&gt;core&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;optional&lt;/strong&gt; subjects that cater to the varied learning needs and interests of our student community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-academic-year-structure&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  🗓️ Academic Year Structure&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-academic-year-structure&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autumn Term&lt;/strong&gt;: Early September to mid-December (Half-term: Late October)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Qur&#39;an</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/quran/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Jun 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/docs/curriculum/quran/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;-quran-curriculum-overview&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  📖 Qur’an Curriculum Overview&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-quran-curriculum-overview&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Our Qur’an programme emphasises &lt;strong&gt;Tajwīd&lt;/strong&gt;, reading fluency, memorisation, and the learning of essential &lt;strong&gt;duʿās&lt;/strong&gt;. Students progress through a carefully structured syllabus from Class 1 to Class 7, allowing them to gradually develop confidence, skill, and a connection with the Qur’an.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;-memorisation-curriculum&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;  🧠 Memorisation Curriculum&#xD;&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#-memorisation-curriculum&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Each class memorises a set of short &lt;strong&gt;Sūrahs&lt;/strong&gt; from &lt;em&gt;Juz ʿAmma&lt;/em&gt;, along with other important verses and Surahs, beginning with those that are easiest to learn. The memorisation schedule is spread across &lt;a href=&#34;https://cambournecrescent.github.io/docs/curriculum/#-academic-year-structure&#34;&gt;three terms&lt;/a&gt; each year. As students progress, they are gradually introduced to longer and more complex Sūrahs suited to their age and ability.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
